  "lineage": "The instrumental climax section of Congolese rumba, isolated and extended from the mid-1970s by Zaiko Langa Langa and then by the Paris-based Kinshasa diaspora of the 1980s around Diblo Dibala, Rigo Star and Kanda Bongo Man: tempo pushed to 130-160 BPM, a rapid ostinato lead-guitar cell repeated over the mi-solo and rhythm guitars, snare-driven kit with the cavacha shuffle and hi-hat sixteenths, shouted animateur commands and dancer-name calls replacing sung verse.",
